    "created_at": "2025-09-07T01:39:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-09-07T01:39:36Z",
    "body": "I wanted to investigate how this issue went unnoticed until now, and instead found that that the issue is already noted right there in the specification; it&#8217;s just noted in such a way that no one can see it.\n\nhttps://searchfox.org/whatwg-html/diff/1048a660579c0ac05b6f483cc6e065b9ffca7f5c/source#98812:\n\n> ```html\n> <!-- Fetch doesn't actually require the value to start with \"Mozilla/5.0 (\". -->\n> ```\n\nThis is commit 1048a660579c0ac05b6f483cc6e065b9ffca7f5c, the same one that introduced this definition of `appVersion`. It wasn&#8217;t just slipped in quietly; it went through issue #7773 and PR #7793, which had some discussion. Why wasn&#8217;t the issue dealt with then, or at least properly marked up as an inline issue so people knew what was going on?\n\nI couldn&#8217;t find a relevant issue in https://github.com/whatwg/fetch. Should there be one?",
