    "created_at": "2025-09-08T12:24:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-09-08T12:24:56Z",
    "body": "1. Do all major browsers use a value that starts with that string? Per https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/User-Agent it seems like yes, except for older Opera browsers.\n2. Is anyone planning to use a different string?\n\nA proposal:\n\n1. We suggest in Fetch that starting with \"Mozilla/5.0 (\" and generally basing it on existing deployed browsers is probably good for compatibility. We don't outright require it for now, though I could be convinced.\n2. We account for it not starting with that by returning the empty string for `appVersion` in such cases.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
