    "created_at": "2025-09-08T22:36:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-09-08T22:36:45Z",
    "body": "For what's worth, [in the WinterTC Minimum Common API](https://min-common-api.proposal.wintertc.org/#navigator-useragent-requirements) we specify that server-side runtimes must support `navigator.userAgent`, and basically recommend against using \"Mozilla/5.0\", since this isn't needed for compatibility in that field, and as far as I can tell no server-side runtime use it.\n\nNow, the Minimum Common API doesn't require runtimes to implement the rest of `navigator`, including `appVersion`; and although runtimes still could, I'd be surprised if any did. But that said, given that there's a subset of implementations of web standards that don't follow this pattern, we should avoid having the standards depend on it.",
